## Lab-Grown Emerald Cut Eternity Band Prices

Lab-grown eternity bands use F-G/VS2-SI1 graded emerald cut diamonds set in a full eternity configuration. The grade range is specific: F-G color keeps the band looking white in any metal, and VS2-SI1 clarity sits high enough that the step-cut tables are clean to the eye. Eternity bands cannot hide inclusions the way a solitaire setting might — each stone is independently visible.

At 3ct total weight in 14K white gold, the starting price in certified market inventory is [$5,000](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/emerald-cut-lab-grown-diamond-eternity-ring-in-14k-white-gold-3-ct-tw-f-g-vs2-si1-item-257651?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). At 11ct total weight, it reaches [$10,820](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/emerald-cut-lab-grown-diamond-eternity-ring-in-14k-white-gold-11-ct-tw-f-g-vs2-si1-item-258099?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). That price range is remarkable for what's on the hand: 11 carats of step-cut diamonds going all the way around the finger for under $11,000.

