The natural vs lab price gap at this end of the market is smaller than most buyers expect. At 2ct total weight, natural prong is $4,815 versus lab prong at $4,640 — a difference of $175. At 11ct, natural is $49,762 versus lab at $10,820 — a $38,942 gap.

The divergence grows because larger individual stones require more natural rarity premium per stone.

> "Eternity bands are where the natural vs lab story gets interesting. At 2ct total weight, the individual stones are tiny — about 0.15 to 0.20 carats each. Natural rarity barely applies at that size. By the time you reach 6ct or 7ct, each stone is larger and the natural premium starts compounding across every stone on the band." — Farzana Hasan

